    }, {
      "text": "\n\n\nAh, this is a brilliant bug! You just hit a classic embedded hardware synchronization issue. I know exactly why you only saw an `\"H\"` and then the entire system froze.\n\n### The Diagnosis: Why did it freeze at \"H\"?\n\nWhen you type `Serial.println(\"Hello...\")` in Arduino C++, the code doesn\u0027t send the whole word instantly. It puts the first letter `\"H\"` into a tiny hardware buffer (a waiting room) and then tells the USART hardware, *\"Hey, transmit this letter. Let me know when you\u0027re done so I can give you the next one.\"*\n\nThe CPU then enters a microscopic `while` loop, checking the USART Status Register, waiting for the \"I\u0027m done sending\" flag.\n\n**Our bug:** In our emulation loop, we ran `avrInstruction(cpu)` which executes the C++ code perfectly. **But we forgot to advance the hardware clock!** Because the hardware clock never ticked, the USART peripheral never finished sending the `\"H\"`. The CPU is trapped in an infinite `while` loop waiting for a hardware event that will never happen.\n\nThe developer of `avr8js` recently updated the library: instead of manually ticking `timer0.tick()` (which threw an error for us earlier), they grouped ALL hardware peripherals (Timers, USART, ADCs) into a single master function called `cpu.tick()`.\n\n### The Fix\n\nOpen your `src/App.jsx`, scroll down to line 92 (inside the `executeFrame` function), and simply add `cpu.tick();` right below `avrInstruction(cpu);`.\n\nIt should look exactly like this:\n\n```javascript\n      const executeFrame \u003d () \u003d\u003e {\n         try {\n            // Run exactly 1 frame of hardware time (16MHz / 60fps)\n            for (let i \u003d 0; i \u003c 266666; i++) {\n              avrInstruction(cpu); \n              cpu.tick(); // \u003c--- ADD THIS LINE! This advances the hardware clock!\n            }\n            requestRef.current \u003d requestAnimationFrame(executeFrame);\n         } catch (e) {\n            setSysLogs(prev \u003d\u003e[...prev, \u0027\u003e FATAL CPU CRASH: \u0027 + e.message]);\n            setIsRunning(false);\n         }\n      };\n```\n\nSave the file, click **RESET**, and then click **RUN**. \n\nBecause `cpu.tick()` is now pulsing the hardware forward, the USART will finish sending \"H\", ask the CPU for \"e\", then \"l\", then \"l\", then \"o\", and `delay(1000)` will actually know how much time has passed! \n\nTell me if you see `\"Running perfectly...\"` printing continuously now!",
      "role": "model",
      "grounding": {
        "webSearchQueries": ["\"avr8js\" execution loop example", "\"avr8js\" timer0.tick", "\"avrInstruction(cpu);\" \"avr8js\" cpu.tick()", "\"cpu.tick()\" \"avr8js\""]
      },
      "finishReason": "STOP",
      "tokenCount": 588,
