      }, {
        "text": "\n  );\n}\n\nexport default App;\n```\n\n### What happens when you run this:\n1. You will see a"
      }, {
        "text": " top-down view of a walled arena, and a blue square (your robot) in the center.\n2. Click **RUN**."
      }, {
        "text": "\n3. The Serial Monitor will say `\"Driving Forward...\"`. The Arduino\u0027s CPU will send an electrical HIGH signal"
      }, {
        "text": " to virtual Pins 9 and 10.\n4. The JavaScript Engine intercepts this electrical signal and applies a physical pushing"
      }, {
        "text": " force to the left and right sides of the blue square, driving it across the canvas!\n5. After 1 second, the"
      }, {
        "text": " Arduino will cut the power. The physics engine reads the LOW signal, stops applying force, and friction brings the robot to a halt."
      }, {
        "text": "\n6. The Arduino will then fire just Pin 9, causing the robot to turn!\n\nTry it out! Click"
      }, {
