      "parts": [{
        "text": "\n\n\nYou caught me again! The brain is working perfectly, but the \"virtual muscles\" were far"
      }, {
        "text": " too weak. \n\nHere is exactly what happened in the background:\n1. **The Air Friction:** In `Matter"
      }, {
        "text": ".js`, I set the `frictionAir` to `0.1`.\n2. **The Force:** I only"
      }, {
        "text": " applied `0.0005` units of force per frame. \nBecause the friction was so high and"
      }, {
        "text": " the force was so low, the virtual robot reached a \"terminal velocity\" of nearly zero. It *was* trying to move, but"
      }, {
        "text": " it was moving by microscopic fractions of a pixel! \n\nOn top of that, I realized my previous geometry code was pushing the front of"
      }, {
        "text": " the square, instead of simulating proper tank-drive steering (Left Motor pushing the left side, Right Motor pushing the right side).\n\n### The"
      }, {
        "text": " Fix \u0026 The \"Wow\" Factor\nWe are going to do two things in this update:\n1. **Fix the Physics \u0026"
      }, {
        "text": " Enforce Determinism:** We will increase the motor torque. We will also force the `Matter.js` engine to"
      }, {
        "text": " step forward by exactly `16.666ms` per frame, ignoring real-world time. This ensures your robot runs identically"
      }, {
        "text": " on every computer.\n2. **The \"Wow\" Factor:** We are going to wire the UI\u0027s text"
      }, {
        "text": " directly to the emulator\u0027s RAM. When Pin 9 goes `HIGH` in your code, the text \"Motor Left: Pin 9"
      }, {
        "text": "\" in your Workshop panel will literally light up bright green in real-time so you can *see* the electricity.\n\n###"
      }, {
        "text": " Step 1: The Master Upgrade\nOpen your `src/App.jsx`, delete everything, and paste this upgraded"
      }, {
        "text": " version:\n\n```jsx\nimport React, { useState, useRef, useEffect } from \u0027react\u0027;\nimport Editor from"
      }, {
        "text": " \u0027@monaco-editor/react\u0027;\nimport { Play, Square, RotateCcw, Monitor, Settings } from"
      }, {
        "text": " \u0027lucide-react\u0027;\nimport Matter from \u0027matter-js\u0027;\nimport { \n  CPU, av"
      }, {
        "text": "rInstruction, \n  AVRTimer, timer0Config, timer1Config, timer2Config,"
      }, {
        "text": " \n  AVRUSART, usart0Config, \n  AVRIOPort, portBConfig, portC"
      }, {
        "text": "Config, portDConfig \n} from \u0027avr8js\u0027;\n\n// --- INTEL HEX PARSER ---"
      }, {
        "text": "\nfunction loadHex(source, target) {\n  for (const line of source.split(\u0027\\n\u0027)) {"
      }, {
        "text": "\n    if (line[0] \u003d\u003d\u003d \u0027:\u0027 \u0026\u0026 line.substring(7, 9) \u003d\u003d\u003d \u002700\u0027)"
      }, {
        "text": " {\n      const bytes \u003d parseInt(line.substring(1, 3), 16);\n      const"
      }, {
        "text": " addr \u003d parseInt(line.substring(3, 7), 16);\n      for (let i \u003d"
      }, {
        "text": " 0; i \u003c bytes; i++) {\n        target[addr + i] \u003d parseInt(line.substring"
      }, {
        "text": "(9 + i * 2, 11 + i * 2), 16);\n      }"
      }, {
        "text": "\n    }\n  }\n}\n\n// --- DEFAULT ROBOT CODE ---\nconst defaultCode \u003d `// HARD"
      }, {
        "text": "WARE PINS\nconst int MOTOR_LEFT \u003d 9;  // Port B, Bit 1\nconst int"
