      }, {
        "text": " App;\n```\n\n### Try it now!\n1. Save the code and let it reload.\n2. Look"
      }, {
        "text": " down at the **Robot Workshop** panel. Notice how the pins have little empty circles next to them `○`.\n3. Click **RUN"
      }, {
        "text": "**.\n4. When the Serial Monitor says `\"Driving Forward...\"`, look at the UI! Both pins will light up bright"
      }, {
        "text": " green, and the blue square will shoot across the screen. \n5. When it says `\"Turning Right...\"`, only the Left"
      }, {
        "text": " Motor pin will be green, and the square will spin on the canvas. \n\nLet me know if it moves!"
      }, {
        "text": " You are basically watching standard C++ code perfectly manipulate a JavaScript physics engine via a 16MHz virtual memory bridge."
      }, {
