        "text": "I"
      }, {
        "text": " see exactly what happened. \n\n**The Root Cause:** `react-resizable-"
      }, {
        "text": "panels` is ruthless when it comes to its children. My previous update had these"
      }, {
        "text": " logical issues:\n1.  I added `// INLINED VERTICAL HANDLE` comments and then *deleted* the helper components. `react-resizable-panels"
      }, {
        "text": "` still saw those as extra code, and silently crashed.\n\n2.  The \"Ghost Canvas Killer\" logic was great for the top-level Canvas, but because"
      }, {
        "text": " of the resizer, React *re-renders the entire simulation field*, including the HUD!\n\n### The True Ultimate Fix: The Immutable HUD\nWe are going to make the HUD\u0027s \"X-Ray\" display a separate, non-"
      }, {
        "text": "resizable `\u003cdiv\u003e` element. That way, even if the user drags the canvas around, React will only update the canvas, not the static HUD elements.\n\nOpen `src/App.jsx`, delete everything, and paste this masterpiece:\n\n```jsx"
      }, {
        "text": "\nimport React, { useState, useRef, useEffect } from \u0027react\u0027;\nimport Editor from \u0027@monaco-editor/react\u0027;\nimport { Play, Square, RotateCcw, Monitor, Settings, Terminal, Crosshair, GripVertical, GripHorizontal } from \u0027lucide-react\u0027;\nimport Matter from"
