      "parts": [{
        "text": "\n\n\nAh, I know exactly what happened! You just discovered a classic JavaScript \"Event Bubbling\" trap."
      }, {
        "text": "\n\n### The Bug: The Icon Trap\nWhen you click and drag the middle slider, it works perfectly. But when you click the bottom"
      }, {
        "text": " sliders, your mouse might accidentally click the **tiny grip icon** inside the slider instead of the slider itself. \n\nIn my code, I"
      }, {
        "text": " used `e.target.parentElement` to calculate the height of the screen. If you accidentally clicked the icon, the"
      }, {
        "text": " math grabbed the height of the *icon\u0027s container* (which is only 8 pixels tall) instead of the"
      }, {
        "text": " whole screen! Dividing your mouse movement by 8 pixels caused the math to output `5000%`, making"
      }, {
        "text": " the UI instantly \"warp\" to its maximum limit.\n\n### The Fix: Target Locking\nWe are going to change"
      }, {
        "text": " `e.target` to `e.currentTarget`. This forces JavaScript to completely ignore the tiny icons and lock the math purely"
      }, {
        "text": " onto the massive screen-height columns.\n\nOpen `src/App.jsx`, delete everything, and paste this warp"
      }, {
        "text": "-free version:\n\n```jsx\nimport React, { useState, useRef, useEffect } from \u0027react\u0027;\nimport"
      }, {
        "text": " Editor from \u0027@monaco-editor/react\u0027;\nimport { Play, Square, RotateCcw, Monitor, Settings"
      }, {
        "text": ", Terminal, Crosshair, GripVertical, GripHorizontal } from \u0027lucide-react\u0027;\nimport Matter from \u0027"
      }, {
        "text": "matter-js\u0027;\nimport { \n  CPU, avrInstruction, \n  AVRTimer, timer"
      }, {
        "text": "0Config, timer1Config, timer2Config, \n  AVRUSART, usart0Config"
      }, {
        "text": " \n} from \u0027avr8js\u0027; \n\n// --- INTEL HEX PARSER ---\nfunction loadHex(source,"
      }, {
        "text": " target) {\n  for (const line of source.split(\u0027\\n\u0027)) {\n    if (line"
      }, {
        "text": "[0] \u003d\u003d\u003d \u0027:\u0027 \u0026\u0026 line.substring(7, 9) \u003d\u003d\u003d \u002700\u0027) {\n      const bytes \u003d"
      }, {
        "text": " parseInt(line.substring(1, 3), 16);\n      const addr \u003d parseInt(line."
      }, {
        "text": "substring(3, 7), 16);\n      for (let i \u003d 0; i \u003c bytes"
      }, {
        "text": "; i++) {\n        target[addr + i] \u003d parseInt(line.substring(9 + i *"
      }, {
        "text": " 2, 11 + i * 2), 16);\n      }\n    }\n  }"
      }, {
        "text": "\n}\n\n// --- DEFAULT ROBOT CODE ---\nconst defaultCode \u003d `// HARDWARE PINS\nconst int"
      }, {
        "text": " MOTOR_LEFT \u003d 9;  // Port B, Bit 1\nconst int MOTOR_RIGHT \u003d 1"
      }, {
        "text": "0; // Port B, Bit 2\n\nvoid setup() {\n  Serial.begin(9600"
      }, {
        "text": ");\n  pinMode(MOTOR_LEFT, OUTPUT);\n  pinMode(MOTOR_RIGHT, OUTPUT);"
      }, {
        "text": "\n  Serial.println(\"Robot Booted. Ready to drive.\");\n}\n\nvoid loop() {\n  Serial."
      }, {
        "text": "println(\"Driving Forward...\");\n  digitalWrite(MOTOR_LEFT, HIGH);\n  digitalWrite(MOTOR_RIGHT"
      }, {
        "text": ", HIGH);\n  delay(1000);\n\n  Serial.println(\"Stopping...\");\n  digitalWrite"
      }, {
        "text": "(MOTOR_LEFT, LOW);\n  digitalWrite(MOTOR_RIGHT, LOW);\n  delay(50"
      }, {
        "text": "0);\n\n  Serial.println(\"Turning Right...\");\n  digitalWrite(MOTOR_LEFT, HIGH);"
      }, {
        "text": "\n  digitalWrite(MOTOR_RIGHT, LOW);\n  delay(1000);\n}`;\n\nfunction App()"
      }, {
        "text": " {\n  const[code, setCode] \u003d useState(defaultCode);\n  const"
      }, {
        "text": "[sysLogs, setSysLogs] \u003d useState([\u0027\u003e System Ready. Waiting for compilation...\u0027]);\n  const"
      }, {
        "text": "[serialOutput, setSerialOutput] \u003d useState(\"\");\n  const[isRunning, setIsRunning] \u003d useState(false);\n  \n  //"
      }, {
        "text": " --- NATIVE RESIZER STATE ---\n  const [leftWidth, setLeftWidth] \u003d useState(45);"
      }, {
        "text": "      \n  const [editorHeight, setEditorHeight] \u003d useState(60); \n  const"
      }, {
        "text": "[canvasHeight, setCanvasHeight] \u003d useState(65); \n  const[isDragging, setIsDragging] \u003d useState(false);"
      }, {
        "text": "  \n  \n  const requestRef \u003d useRef(null);\n  const sysLogEndRef \u003d useRef(null);"
      }, {
        "text": "\n  const serialEndRef \u003d useRef(null);\n  \n  const sceneRef \u003d useRef(null);"
      }, {
        "text": "\n  const engineRef \u003d useRef(null);\n  const robotRef \u003d useRef(null);\n  const runnerRef \u003d"
      }, {
        "text": " useRef(null); \n  const mouseConstraintRef \u003d useRef(null); \n\n  useEffect(() \u003d\u003e {"
      }, {
        "text": "\n    sysLogEndRef.current?.scrollIntoView({ behavior: \"smooth\" });\n  },"
      }, {
        "text": "[sysLogs]);\n\n  useEffect(() \u003d\u003e {\n    serialEndRef.current?.scrollIntoView({ behavior: \"smooth\""
      }, {
        "text": " });\n  },[serialOutput]);\n\n  // --- BULLETPROOF NATIVE DRAG HANDLERS ---"
      }, {
        "text": "\n  const handleDragMain \u003d (e) \u003d\u003e {\n    e.preventDefault();\n    setIsDragging(true);"
      }, {
        "text": "\n    // currentTarget ALWAYS locks onto the handle, never the child icon\n    const container \u003d e.currentTarget.parentElement;"
      }, {
        "text": " \n    const { left, width } \u003d container.getBoundingClientRect();\n    const onMouseMove \u003d (ev)"
      }, {
        "text": " \u003d\u003e {\n      setLeftWidth(Math.max(20, Math.min(80, ((ev"
      }, {
        "text": ".clientX - left) / width) * 100)));\n    };\n    const onMouseUp \u003d"
      }, {
        "text": " () \u003d\u003e {\n      setIsDragging(false);\n      document.removeEventListener(\u0027mousemove\u0027, onMouseMove);"
      }, {
        "text": "\n      document.removeEventListener(\u0027mouseup\u0027, onMouseUp);\n    };\n    document.addEventListener(\u0027mousemove\u0027, onMouseMove"
      }, {
        "text": ");\n    document.addEventListener(\u0027mouseup\u0027, onMouseUp);\n  };\n\n  const handleDragEditor \u003d ("
      }, {
        "text": "e) \u003d\u003e {\n    e.preventDefault();\n    setIsDragging(true);\n    const container \u003d e."
      }, {
        "text": "currentTarget.parentElement;\n    const { top, height } \u003d container.getBoundingClientRect();\n    const onMouseMove \u003d"
      }, {
        "text": " (ev) \u003d\u003e {\n      setEditorHeight(Math.max(20, Math.min(80"
      }, {
        "text": ", ((ev.clientY - top) / height) * 100)));\n    };\n    const on"
      }, {
