      "parts": [{
        "text": "\n\n\nThis is the hallmark of professional software. You need a way"
      }, {
        "text": " to build your perfect workspace, lock your robot\u0027s starting position, and have the software remember it completely. \n\nSince"
      }, {
        "text": " web browsers don\u0027t allow applications to silently read and write to your local hard drive (for security reasons), we are going to build"
      }, {
        "text": " a **Hybrid Save System**:\n\n1. **The Auto-Save Cache (localStorage):** Every time you resize a window,"
      }, {
        "text": " drag the robot, or apply a teleport, the app will instantly save those settings to your browser\u0027s internal cache. If you refresh the"
      }, {
        "text": " page or close the tab, everything will automatically be exactly where you left it.\n2. **The Hard-File Export:** I have added"
      }, {
        "text": " \"Export Config\" and \"Import Config\" buttons to the Robot Workshop. This allows you to literally download a `.json` file"
      }, {
        "text": " of your setup to your computer, share it with another student, or back it up!\n3. **The \"Oops"
      }, {
        "text": "\" Button:** I added a \"Restore Default\" button in case you mess up your layout and want to reset it to"
      }, {
        "text": " the factory 200x200 starting position.\n\n### The Auto-Save / Config File Update\n\nOpen `src/App"
      }, {
        "text": ".jsx`, delete everything, and paste this master version:\n\n```jsx\nimport React, { useState, useRef, useEffect } from \u0027react"
