        "text": "\u0027ve hit on a critical point: when we upload an image, how do"
      }, {
        "text": " we tell the physics engine to scale and position it correctly? Right now, it\u0027s just blasting the image onto the canvas, and the Matter.js world is still operating in its own coordinate system.\n\nTo fix this, we need"
      }, {
        "text": " to:\n1. **Image Scaling:** When an image is uploaded, we need to read its `naturalWidth` and `naturalHeight`. We then tell the Matter.js engine to scale its world dimensions to match these natural pixel dimensions. "
      }, {
        "text": "\n2. **Coordinate System Alignment:** We need to make sure that `0,0` in the Matter.js world corresponds to the top-left corner of the image. \n3. **HUD Relocation:** We will move the entire"
      }, {
        "text": " \"SYS_TELEMETRY \u0026 MANUAL POSE\" block to be a header for the \"Robot Workshop\" section, making the canvas area cleaner.\n\n### The Pixel-Perfect, Deterministic Positioning Update\n\nOpen `src/App.jsx"
      }, {
        "text": "`, delete everything, and paste this updated version:\n\n```jsx\nimport React, { useState, useRef, useEffect } from \u0027react\u0027;\nimport Editor from \u0027@monaco-editor/react\u0027;\nimport { Play, Square, Rotate"
      }, {
