      "parts": [{
        "text": "\n\n\nYou have an incredible eye for debugging. You"
      }, {
        "text": " just correctly diagnosed a **Main Thread Bottleneck**. \n\nWhen the Code Editor (Monaco) lags, it means"
      }, {
        "text": " the browser\u0027s JavaScript engine is choking so hard on the simulation math that it doesn\u0027t even have time to register your keyboard presses"
      }, {
        "text": ". The \"4 pixels per frame\" looked like lag because your browser\u0027s frame rate plummeted from a smooth 60 FPS down to a"
      }, {
        "text": " choppy 15 FPS!\n\n### The Two Villains Causing the Lag:\n1. **The Serial Monitor Trap ("
      }, {
        "text": "The worst offender):** I programmed the `USART` hardware to update the React UI every time it received a byte. The"
      }, {
        "text": " phrase `\"Driving Forward...\"` is 18 letters long. That means in a single frame, the emulator was telling React to redraw"
      }, {
        "text": " the entire screen **18 separate times!** This completely crippled the browser.\n2. **The Overclocked Loop:** Our"
      }, {
        "text": " `for` loop was running exactly `266,666` *instructions* per frame. But in Arduino"
      }, {
        "text": " hardware, an instruction usually takes 2 or 3 *clock cycles* to complete. We were accidentally simulating the robot"
      }, {
        "text": " at 30MHz instead of 16MHz, doing double the math required!\n\n### The \"60 FPS"
      }, {
        "text": " Butter Smooth\" Fix\nWe are going to do two things:\n1. **The Serial Buffer:** We will collect all the"
      }, {
        "text": " letters into a temporary hidden string, and only tell React to update the screen *once* at the very end of the"
      }, {
        "text": " frame.\n2. **The Cycle Counter:** We will ask the `avrInstruction` exactly how many cycles it used, and increment"
      }, {
        "text": " our loop by that number. This instantly cuts the emulator\u0027s CPU load in half.\n\nOpen `src/App"
      }, {
        "text": ".jsx`, delete everything, and paste this highly optimized, butter-smooth version:\n\n```jsx\nimport React, { useState"
      }, {
        "text": ", useRef, useEffect } from \u0027react\u0027;\nimport Editor from \u0027@monaco-editor/react\u0027;\nimport {"
      }, {
        "text": " Play, Square, RotateCcw, Monitor, Settings, Terminal, Crosshair, GripVertical, GripHorizontal, Download"
      }, {
        "text": ", Upload, RefreshCcw, FileUp, ImagePlus, Trash2 } from \u0027lucide-react\u0027;"
      }, {
        "text": "\nimport Matter from \u0027matter-js\u0027;\nimport { \n  CPU, avrInstruction, \n  AV"
      }, {
        "text": "RTimer, timer0Config, timer1Config, timer2Config, \n  AVRUSART, usart"
      }, {
        "text": "0Config \n} from \u0027avr8js\u0027; \n\nfunction loadHex(source, target) {"
      }, {
        "text": "\n  for (const line of source.split(\u0027\\n\u0027)) {\n    if (line[0] \u003d\u003d\u003d \u0027:\u0027 \u0026\u0026 line"
      }, {
        "text": ".substring(7, 9) \u003d\u003d\u003d \u002700\u0027) {\n      const bytes \u003d parseInt(line.substring"
      }, {
        "text": "(1, 3), 16);\n      const addr \u003d parseInt(line.substring(3,"
      }, {
        "text": " 7), 16);\n      for (let i \u003d 0; i \u003c bytes; i++) {"
      }, {
        "text": "\n        target[addr + i] \u003d parseInt(line.substring(9 + i * 2, 11"
      }, {
        "text": " + i * 2), 16);\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n\nconst DEFAULT"
      }, {
        "text": "_CONFIG \u003d {\n  leftWidth: 45,\n  editorHeight: 60,"
      }, {
        "text": "\n  canvasHeight: 65,\n  robotX: 200,\n  robotY: 2"
      }, {
        "text": "00,\n  robotAngle: 0 \n};\n\nconst getConfig \u003d () \u003d\u003e {\n  try {"
      }, {
        "text": "\n    const saved \u003d localStorage.getItem(\u0027flawless-config\u0027);\n    if (saved) return { ...DEFAULT_CONFIG, ...JSON."
