        "text": "\n\n\nThis is the ultimate evolution of a robotics simulator. You don\u0027t just want a code emulator anymore"
      }, {
        "text": "; you want **Kerbal Space Program** or **Besiege** for Arduino!\n\nBefore we code this, we"
      }, {
        "text": " need to have a quick architectural reality check:\n\n### The 3D vs. 2D Dilemma\nGoing"
      }, {
        "text": " **full 3D** (using something like `Three.js` or React Three Fiber) would require completely throwing away our"
      }, {
        "text": " `Matter.js` physics engine and starting from scratch. Full 3D also introduces Z-axis physics (gravity"
      }, {
        "text": ", tipping over, camera angles), which makes guaranteeing \"100% determinism\" incredibly difficult in a web browser.\n\n**However,"
      }, {
        "text": " we can build a \"Top-Down Modular 2D Sandbox\"** (Think of games like *RimWorld*, *"
      }, {
        "text": "Factorio*, or *Prison Architect*). \n\nWe can create a **\"Garage Mode\"** where:\n1. You see a top"
      }, {
        "text": "-down view of your raw \"Chassis\" (the blue block).\n2. You have an inventory drawer of parts"
      }, {
        "text": " (Wheels, Sonar, IR Sensors, LEDs).\n3. You drag a Wheel and snap it to the left"
      }, {
        "text": " side. You drag a Sonar and stick it on the front.\n4. **The Physics adapt:** If you place the wheels"
      }, {
        "text": " all the way at the back of the chassis instead of the center, the robot will drive and turn completely differently because the *"
      }, {
        "text": "Center of Mass* and *Torque Offsets* dynamically shift!\n\n### How we will build this (The Blueprint"
      }, {
        "text": "):\n\n**Step 1: The Component Data Structure**\nInstead of the robot being a single hardcoded rectangle, it becomes a JavaScript Array"
      }, {
