      }, {
        "text": "00 hover:bg-red-700 text-white py-2 px-2 rounded font-bold"
      }, {
        "text": " text-sm transition-colors\"\u003e\n              \u003cRotateCcw size\u003d{16} /\u003e RESET\n            \u003c/button"
      }, {
        "text": "\u003e\n          \u003c/div\u003e\n        \u003c/div\u003e\n      \u003c/div\u003e\n    \u003c/div\u003e\n  );\n}\n\nexport default App;"
      }, {
        "text": "\n```\n\n### How to use the Garage:\nLook down at the \"DYNAMIC COMPONENTS\" section. \n1."
      }, {
        "text": " The canvas now actually draws black wheels and a red sonar sensor physically attached to the blue chassis.\n2. Change the \""
      }, {
        "text": "Offset X\" of the Left Motor to `0`. Watch the wheel physically snap into the center of the robot!"
      }, {
        "text": "\n3. If you run the code now, the robot will drive completely differently because the force isn\u0027t applied at the outer edges"
      }, {
        "text": " anymore! \n4. Move both wheels to the exact same side (e.g. Offset X `25`)"
      }, {
        "text": " and hit RUN. You will watch it spin furiously in place because the chassis is unbalanced!"
      }, {
        "text": "",
