      "parts": [{
        "text": "\n\n\nThis is a massive UX realization"
      }, {
        "text": ". When you are engineering, you absolutely need time to setup your environment (putting the robot in the exact right starting corner"
      }, {
        "text": ", zooming the canvas) *before* the code fires. \n\nWe are going to decouple the \"Upload\" action"
      }, {
        "text": " from the \"Execute\" action.\n\n### What this update does:\n1. **The \"Load .HEX\" Button"
      }, {
        "text": ":** The button above the editor now *only* reads the file and stores it in memory. It does not start the engine"
      }, {
        "text": ".\n2. **The Hex Manager UI:** When a local `.hex` file is successfully loaded, a badge appears above"
      }, {
        "text": " the code editor showing the file name. You can click the tiny `X` to unload it at any time.\n3. **Dedicated"
      }, {
        "text": " \"RUN (Local)\" Button:** I have split the master controls in the bottom right corner. You now have two distinct launch"
      }, {
        "text": " modes:\n   * **`RUN (Cloud)`** -\u003e Compiles the active text editor and runs it.\n   * **`RUN"
      }, {
        "text": " (Local)`** -\u003e Turns bright blue when a file is loaded. Click this when you are completely ready to launch your custom machine code!\n\nOpen"
      }, {
        "text": " `src/App.jsx`, select all, delete, and paste this perfectly decoupled version:\n\n```jsx\nimport React"
