      "parts": [{
        "text": "\n\n\nThis is a classic \"React State vs. Physics Engine\""
      }, {
        "text": " desync bug! \n\n### The Diagnosis: The Teleporting Crate\nWhen you dragged the object with your mouse, the"
      }, {
        "text": " `Matter.js` physics engine moved the physical box on the screen, and I used a high-speed DOM injection to update"
      }, {
        "text": " the `X` and `Y` input boxes so it wouldn\u0027t lag the browser.\n\n**However**, to"
      }, {
        "text": " save performance, I didn\u0027t push those new coordinates into the *React State array* immediately. \nSo when you clicked the"
      }, {
        "text": " `Fixed Wall` checkbox, React said: *\"Oh, the user changed a setting! Let me rebuild the physics engine using"
      }, {
        "text": " the coordinates I have in my memory.\"* Since React still had the *old* coordinates from before you dragged it, it instantly teleported the box back"
      }, {
        "text": " in time!\n\n### The \"Physics Snapshot\" Fix\nWe are going to upgrade the `updateArenaObject` function"
      }, {
        "text": ". Before React applies the `Fixed Wall` setting, it will take a lightning-fast \"snapshot\" of the live"
      }, {
        "text": " physics engine. It will grab the *true* physical `X`, `Y`, and `Angle` of every single box on the screen, merge"
      }, {
        "text": " it into its memory, and *then* apply the checkbox. \n\nThis completely cures the teleporting bug, and also ensures that if"
      }, {
        "text": " your robot crashes into a crate and pushes it across the room, ticking the checkbox will lock it down exactly where the robot pushed"
      }, {
        "text": " it!\n\nOpen `src/App.jsx`, select all, delete, and paste this locked-in version:\n\n```jsx"
      }, {
        "text": "\nimport React, { useState, useRef, useEffect } from \u0027react\u0027;\nimport Editor from \u0027@monaco-editor/"
      }, {
        "text": "react\u0027;\nimport { Play, Square, RotateCcw, Monitor, Settings, Terminal, Crosshair, GripVertical"
      }, {
        "text": ", GripHorizontal, Download, Upload, RefreshCcw, FileUp, ImagePlus, Trash2, Wrench,"
      }, {
        "text": " PlusCircle, X, Box } from \u0027lucide-react\u0027;\nimport Matter from \u0027matter-js\u0027;"
      }, {
        "text": "\nimport { \n  CPU, avrInstruction, \n  AVRTimer, timer0Config, timer1"
      }, {
        "text": "Config, timer2Config, \n  AVRUSART, usart0Config \n} from \u0027avr8"
      }, {
        "text": "js\u0027; \n\nfunction loadHex(source, target) {\n  for (const line of source.split(\u0027\\"
      }, {
        "text": "n\u0027)) {\n    if (line[0] \u003d\u003d\u003d \u0027:\u0027 \u0026\u0026 line.substring(7, 9) \u003d\u003d\u003d"
      }, {
        "text": " \u002700\u0027) {\n      const bytes \u003d parseInt(line.substring(1, 3), 16"
      }, {
        "text": ");\n      const addr \u003d parseInt(line.substring(3, 7), 16);\n      for"
      }, {
        "text": " (let i \u003d 0; i \u003c bytes; i++) {\n        target[addr + i] \u003d parseInt"
      }, {
        "text": "(line.substring(9 + i * 2, 11 + i * 2), 16"
      }, {
        "text": ");\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n\nconst getPinState \u003d (cpu, pin) \u003d\u003e"
      }, {
        "text": " {\n  let portAddr, bit;\n  if (pin \u003e\u003d 0 \u0026\u0026 pin \u003c\u003d 7) {"
      }, {
        "text": " portAddr \u003d 0x2B; bit \u003d pin; } \n  else if (pin \u003e\u003d 8"
      }, {
        "text": " \u0026\u0026 pin \u003c\u003d 13) { portAddr \u003d 0x25; bit \u003d pin - 8;"
      }, {
        "text": " } \n  else if (pin \u003e\u003d 14 \u0026\u0026 pin \u003c\u003d 19) { portAddr \u003d"
      }, {
        "text": " 0x28; bit \u003d pin - 14; } \n  else { return false; }"
      }, {
        "text": "\n  return (cpu.data[portAddr] \u0026 (1 \u003c\u003c bit)) !\u003d\u003d 0;\n};\n\nconst"
      }, {
        "text": " generateId \u003d () \u003d\u003e Math.random().toString(36).substr(2, 9);\n\nconst TYPE"
      }, {
        "text": "_TAGS \u003d {\n  dc_motor: \u0027DC MOTOR\u0027,\n  imu: \u0027IMU\u0027,"
      }, {
        "text": "\n  ir_sensor: \u0027IR SENSOR\u0027,\n  servo: \u0027SERVO\u0027,\n  sonar: \u0027SON"
      }, {
        "text": "AR\u0027\n};\n\nconst DEFAULT_CONFIG \u003d {\n  leftWidth: 45,\n  editorHeight"
      }, {
        "text": ": 60,\n  canvasHeight: 65,\n  robotX: 200,"
      }, {
        "text": "\n  robotY: 200,\n  robotAngle: 0,\n  baudRate: \""
      }, {
        "text": "9600\",\n  robotBuild: {\n    chassisW: 50,\n    ch"
      }, {
        "text": "assisH: 30, \n    parts:"
      }, {
        "text": ""
      }, {
        "text": ""
      }, {
        "text": ""
      }, {
        "text": ""
